WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.883
Think about the temperature outside.

2
00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:11.260
It is 4 degrees.

3
00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:17.927
It gets colder... now it is zero.

4
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.186
It gets even colder. Now it is minus 3.

5
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.093
Numbers below zero are called negative numbers.

6
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.435
On a number line, zero is in the middle.

7
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:37.383
Negative numbers are on the left.

8
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.364
Positive numbers are on the right.

9
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:47.002
Which is bigger: negative five, or negative two?

10
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.672
Further right means bigger.

11
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:58.150
Negative two is bigger. It is warmer than negative five!

12
00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:05.127
Adding means move right. Taking away means move left.

13
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.537
Start at 2. Take away 5: move left 5.

14
00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.132
We land on negative three.

15
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.722
Start at negative four. Add six: move right six.

16
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.207
We land on 2.

17
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.476
Sometimes there are two signs together.

18
00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:40.068
Adding a negative is the same as taking away.

19
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.017
Start at 3. Move left 5.

20
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.505
We land on negative two.

21
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.194
Taking away a negative is the same as adding!

22
00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.303
Start at 1. Move right 3.

23
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.593
We land on 4.

24
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.889
Two minus signs together make a plus.
